---
import Studio from "../../layouts/Studio.astro";
import RelatedPosts from "../../components/RelatedPosts.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, CALENDLY_URL, fmtDate, iso, POSTS } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";

const slug = "how-indian-businesses-use-ai-2026";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Divyansh Sood", url: `${SITE}/`, "@id": `${SITE}/#person` },
      publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": `${SITE}/#studio`,
        name: "Divyansh Sood® Studio",
        logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/icon.svg` },
      },
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      wordCount: post.wordCount,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Studio
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="post-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img src={post.coverImage} alt={post.coverAlt ?? post.title} width="1200" height="750" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
<p>There's a gap between the AI conversation happening in Indian business media and the AI actually running inside Indian small businesses. The media version is about transformation. The real version is quieter, narrower, and considerably more useful.</p>
<p>Here's what I see working, from the businesses I build for — travel operators, schools, contractors, retailers, D2C brands.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-is-actually-in-use">What's actually in daily use</h2>
<h3 id="writing-in-two-languages">Writing, in two languages</h3>
<p>Overwhelmingly the most common real use, and almost nobody calls it "using AI." Product descriptions, enquiry replies, festival campaign copy, translating a page into Hindi without paying for a translator each time. The pattern is always a draft that a person edits — which is exactly the right pattern, and it works.</p>
<h3 id="making-sense-of-messy-input">Turning messy input into structured data</h3>
<p>The most valuable and least discussed. A school receiving admission enquiries in a dozen formats. A contractor with quotes across WhatsApp, email and paper. Getting that into a spreadsheet automatically removes a task someone does by hand daily — and unlike a chatbot, its value is immediately measurable in hours.</p>
<h3 id="the-twenty-questions">Answering the same twenty questions</h3>
<p>Every business has them — check-in time, fee structure, whether you deliver to a particular district. Worth automating <em>once your content is good enough to answer from</em>. I've written the honest version of when this is and isn't worth it in <a href="/blog/ai-chatbot-for-indian-business/">should your Indian business add an AI chatbot</a>.</p>
<h3 id="being-found-by-assistants">Being found by AI assistants at all</h3>
<p>This is the one most Indian businesses haven't registered yet. A meaningful share of buyers now ask an assistant "best taxi service in Kangra" or "schools in Ladwara with a science stream" instead of searching. If your business isn't legible to those systems, you're invisible in a channel that didn't exist three years ago.</p>
<p>It's also the cheapest thing on this list — structured data, clear factual pages, an <a href="/blog/what-is-llms-txt-blog/">llms.txt file</a>. <a href="/projects/baglamukhi-travels/">Baglamukhi Travels</a> ships all three and averages position 5.7 on Google against aggregators with far bigger budgets.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-is-mostly-theatre">What's mostly theatre</h2>
<p><strong>"AI-powered" as a selling point to customers.</strong> Your customer wants a fast site, a clear price and a quick reply. Nobody chose a taxi operator because the website had AI.</p>
<p><strong>Chatbots on sites with no traffic.</strong> Very common, and it's solving the last problem in the funnel while the first one is on fire. If nobody arrives, nothing that happens on the page matters.</p>
<p><strong>Automating a process nobody had defined.</strong> Automation makes a good process faster and a bad process faster at being bad. If nobody can describe the current steps, that's the project — not the software.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-real-advantage">The advantage small businesses actually have</h2>
<p>The genuine shift isn't that Indian small businesses can now do what large companies do. It's that the gap in <em>execution quality</em> narrowed sharply.</p>
<p>A single-owner operator can now publish content as well-written as a company with a marketing team, answer enquiries in two languages, and produce a site as fast and as well-structured as a much larger competitor's. Those advantages used to be bought with headcount.</p>
<p>What hasn't changed: knowing which customer to serve, what to say to them, and being trustworthy when they arrive. Those are still the job, and they're still the difference between businesses that do well and businesses that don't.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="where-to-start">Where I'd start, in order</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Fix the foundation first.</strong> A fast, findable site with a clear path to contact you. Nothing on this list matters if this is broken — and for most businesses it is.</li>
<li><strong>Automate the one task you repeat most.</strong> Not the most impressive one. The one that eats an hour every day. Usually it's turning messages into a list.</li>
<li><strong>Make yourself legible to assistants.</strong> Cheap, mostly technical, and the competitive window is still open in most Indian categories.</li>
<li><strong>Only then consider a customer-facing assistant</strong> — and only if the questions genuinely keep coming.</li>
</ol>
<p>That order is deliberately unexciting. It's also the order in which the money actually comes back.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I'm Divyansh Sood, a web developer in Himachal Pradesh building custom-coded websites for Indian businesses, with <a href="/services/ai-development/">AI features</a> where they earn their place. If you're wondering which of these is worth doing for your business first, <a href="https://wa.me/919816091875">WhatsApp me</a> — I'll give you an honest order of operations, even if it means telling you to skip the AI part.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <RelatedPosts slug={slug} audience={post.audience} />

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={CALENDLY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Studio>
